{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0425","billNumberShort":"H.B. 425","billNumberLong":"HB0425","fileNumber":"2026FL0809","shortTitle":"Local Government Fees Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"PETERK","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Peterson, Karen M.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"BRAMMB","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Brammer, Brady","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies and enacts provisions related to municipal and county fees.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits a city from imposing a fee on the general public for broadband or public safety service, with exceptions;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits a town from imposing a fee on the general public for public safety services, with exceptions;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a municipality or a county to impose a transportation utility fee; <hr><ltbullet>establishes the process and requirements for a municipality or county to impose or increase a transportation utility fee;<hr><ltbullet>establishes the process and requirements for a municipality or county to use the revenue generated by a transportation utility fee;<hr><ltbullet>requires a municipality or county that establishes a transportation utility fee to:<hr><ltbullet1>establish an appeal process; and<hr><ltbullet1>conduct an annual review of the fee;<hr><ltbullet>provides that an ordinance imposing a transportation utility fee is subject to local referenda; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"RuthAnne Oakey-Frost","fiscalAnalyst":"Timothy Kevin Bereece","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"BVXLVCQPVQ","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-29 10:14:13.777","